  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 724 PM EDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nBy Saturday, the upper ridge will cover the southern two-thirds of \nthe CONUS with the center of the upper high near New Mexico and the \nTexas Panhandle. This will keep CAA in the Lower Ohio Valley until \nSunday. Highs will be limited to the mid to upper 80s. \n\nSunday, the upper high gets pushed farther east over the Ozarks and \nnorthern Texas. The surface high moves east of Kentucky with a low \napproaching from the Plains, resulting in WAA returning. We remain \ndry as temperatures increase into the low 90s. \n\nFor the rest of the week, the upper ridge slides directly over the \nOhio Valley with surface high pressure parked over the Southeast. \nContinued WAA and mostly clear skies will help temperatures climb \ninto the mid 90s with dew points in the mid to upper 60s.",
